  [
    id 67
    label "jfyAl4de-To"
    step 0
    date "2020-05-10T12:56:38Z"
    title "The ONLY Baby Formula I Would Give My Child...And Which Ones To Avoid!"
    description "Wow, I did a deep dive on infant and baby formula since it has been a popular request and the news is not good friends. I really can't find ANY formulas on the market that have fantastic ingredients from start to finish, and that's a shame. The reason why I recommend Loulouka is because it's the CLEANEST formula on the market, but still not perfect because of the processed plant based oils they use. 95% of the baby formulas on the market use non-organic GMO milk, added sugar or corn syrup, and nasty palm or soybean oil! Some of these ingredients are bad news, but especially for infants...they must be avoided! Mad love..Bobby, Dessi, Rose, and Art! XOXO&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Check out our Keto Cookbook: https://amzn.to/2TOHWJL&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Loulouka formula: https://organicstart.com/loulouka/stage-1/product?aff=407&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Super nutrition baby book: https://amzn.to/3bkodJW&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Electrolyte drops: https://amzn.to/2KVLOXL&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Formula recipe: https://www.westonaprice.org/health-topics/childrens-health/formula-homemade-baby-formula/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Top formula comparison chart: https://organicstart.com/comparison-chart/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Bone broth recipe:&amp;#10;2-3 pounds organic grass-fed beef bones&amp;#10;2 stalks celery, cleaned &amp;#38; halved&amp;#10;2 large carrot, cleaned &amp;#38; halved&amp;#10;1.5 tablespoons raw apple cider vinegar &amp;#10;Filtered water&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Roast the frozen bones for 15 minutes at 400F. Place everything in the instant pot or pressure cooker and fill wit enough water to reach the maximum line. Pressure cook on high for 3 hours. Carefully release the pressure, I take the pot outside and do this so the kitchen doesn't smell. Strain broth and save bones for another use. Let cool to room temperature, you may have to wait overnight. Store in fridge for 5 days or freeze for 6 moths. Once cooled you need to remove the fat layer on top of the broth. Make another batch with the same bones and add two new ones to the pot. &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Follow Me On Social Media: &amp;#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/flavcity &amp;#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/flavcity &amp;#10;Twitter: https://www.twitter.com/flavcity"
    channeltitle "FlavCity with Bobby Parrish"
    channelid "UCnq1w-56tAvMdDup-CL6Vtg"
