  [
    id 129
    label "o970hNo15G0"
    step 0
    date "2022-05-13T22:37:18Z"
    title "Parents nationwide struggle with a critical baby formula shortage"
    description "A baby formula shortage has become a major problem for parents around the U.S., one without quick solutions. About 40 percent of formula is out of stock nationwide due to supply chain disruptions, inflation and a recall by one of the biggest producers. Meanwhile, the White House announced steps to address the shortage. Brian Dittmeier, of the National WIC Association, joins Ali Rogin to discuss.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Stream your PBS favorites with the PBS app:&amp;#160;https://to.pbs.org/2Jb8twG&amp;#10;Find more from PBS NewsHour at&amp;#160;https://www.pbs.org/newshour&amp;#10;Subscribe to our YouTube channel:&amp;#160;https://bit.ly/2HfsCD6&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Follow us:&amp;#10;Facebook:&amp;#160;http://www.pbs.org/newshour&amp;#10;Twitter:&amp;#160;http://www.twitter.com/newshour&amp;#10;Instagram:&amp;#160;http://www.instagram.com/newshour&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Subscribe:&amp;#10;PBS NewsHour podcasts:&amp;#160;https://www.pbs.org/newshour/podcasts&amp;#10;Newsletters:&amp;#160;https://www.pbs.org/newshour/subscribe"
