  [
    id 494
    label "2n7Uihuwpo4"
    step 0
    date "2022-05-20T01:00:01Z"
    title "This Baby Formula Shortage Is Turning Some into Heroes And Others Into MONSTERS"
    description "Subscribe For Daily PDS News Clips: https://www.youtube.com/c/roguerocket?sub_confirmation=1&amp;#10;Thanks to our sponsor Coinbase. Go to http://coinbasedefranco.com to sign up and get $10 in free Bitcoin!&amp;#10;Watch The Full DeFranco News Show: https://www.youtube.com/defranco?sub_confirmation=1&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;And then, this baby formula shortage is causing mayhem around the country right now as people desperately searching through empty shelves, With this crisis bringing out both the best and the worst in humanity, so first, let&amp;#8217;s start with the worst. And that&amp;#8217;s beautifully exemplified by this video that&amp;#8217;s caught traction between two mothers. And it&amp;#8217;s not surprising people are getting this scared; the shortage is expected to last for weeks or months, and for some it&amp;#8217;s the difference between life and death. Like these two children in Memphis, a toddler and a preschooler, who have been hospitalized because they can&amp;#8217;t get their specialty formula, Which they need because they have short bowel syndrome, a condition that prevents them from absorbing full-sized proteins and affects about 25 in 100,000 children. With Abbott Nutrition, which set off this whole shortage, previously producing around 80% of the specialty formula. So you have one of the kids getting discharged after about a week, but the other, who&amp;#8217;s been there since April, still needing treatment. But then we&amp;#8217;re also seeing the best of humanity coming out of Dallas, that southern hospitality on display.With this 51-year-old restaurant owner named Benji doing what at first appeared to be the most appalling, morally criminal thing you could do,&amp;#10;Buying up 56 cases of baby formula from the distributor that normally supplies his business, cleaning out its stock. And initially planning to resell it at cost, he posted an announcement on the restaurant&amp;#8217;s Facebook page, But when one of the first customers, a mother, showed up crying, telling him she&amp;#8217;s so grateful he ended her frantic search for formula, he changed his mind.  Giving it to her without charge, and then as he explains, &amp;#8220;I said, &amp;#8216;what the heck, [expletive] with it, I&amp;#8217;m just going to give it away free.&amp;#8217;&amp;#8221; [Quote same link] And he did, dishing out all 56 cases in less than an hour to hundreds of people like an angel descending from the heavens to bless the inhabitants of the Earth with milk. But he didn&amp;#8217;t stop there, why not go from angel to god. So he restocks, buying 12 more cases, and when those flew off the shelf just as quick, he buys 20 more, giving those away too. Spending about $3,700 of his own money in total, then explaining, &amp;#8220;The moms, the dads not knowing &amp;#8212; are they going to be able to feed their babies? And it makes me sad to think &amp;#8212; because my kids all eat solid foods now &amp;#8212; but man, not knowing if they can eat would be scary.&amp;#8221; So we&amp;#8217;ve got the best and the worst, now we turn to the politicians. Because amazingly enough, both parties are actually coming together to do something about this. With the House passing two bills last night, One of them giving the Agriculture secretary the ability to waive certain limits on the brands and quantities of formula poor mothers can buy using the special supplemental nutrition program. Also requiring formula manufacturers have contingency plans to deal with recalls in the future. And the second bill provides an extra 28 million dollars to the FDA to get fraudulent formula products off store shelves and boost inspection staff as well as the workforce focused on formula. &amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212; &amp;#10;Produced by: Cory Ray &amp;#10;Edited by: James Girardier, Julie Goldberg, Maxwell Enright&amp;#10;Art Department: William Crespo&amp;#10;Writing/Research: Philip DeFranco, Maddie Crichton&amp;#10;Production Team: Zack Taylor, Emma Leid&amp;#10;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8212;&amp;#10;#DeFranco  #BabyFormula #FormulaShortage"
    channeltitle "PDS News Clips"
    channelid "UCpLB7kBu9O5dbBKhaIOmqcQ"
