    title "What does Baby formula and Snake venom have in common?"
    description "Please go watch my Rumble video:&amp;#10;uploaded today 5/15/2022 which will &amp;#10;expand on this video.&amp;#10;https://rumble.com/v14ufmd-baby-formula-snake-venom-covid-vaccine-symptoms.html &amp;#10;&amp;#10;I share all the links there as well. &amp;#10;For those who are aware of the &amp;#10;baby formula supply chains being &amp;#10;greatly BOTTLEnecked....&amp;#10;  &amp;#34;Septicemia&amp;#34; is a bacteria found in snakes.&amp;#10;Babys who have been killed also died from &amp;#34;Septicemia&amp;#34;&amp;#10;and I found it interesting how the renaming of the&amp;#10;formerly labeled: &amp;#34;Enterobacter sakazakii&amp;#34; was &amp;#10;changed to &amp;#34;Cronobacter sakazakii&amp;#34;  &amp;#10;Now why would they feel the need to rename&amp;#10;this?&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#34;Cronobacter sakazakii, which before 2007 was named Enterobacter sakazakii, is an opportunistic Gram-negative, rod-shaped, pathogenic bacterium...&amp;#34; (link below)&amp;#10;&amp;#34;Enterobacter sakazakii, a rare cause of bloodstream and central nervous system infections..&amp;#34; &amp;#10;https://www.foodsafetynews.com/2009/09/the-naming-of-cronobacter-sakazakii/ &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Septicemia in snakes:&amp;#10;https://netvet.co.uk/exotic/snakes/septicemia/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Septicemia in infants: &amp;#10;https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/cronobacter-sakazakii&amp;#10;Cronobacter sakazakii, enterobacter sakazakii&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Renaming of the &amp;#34;bacteria&amp;#34; https://www.cdc.gov/cronobacter/technical.html &amp;#10;Cronobacter multi-species complex (formerly Enterobacter sakazakii) &amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The reason why SNAKES seem to keep popping up is because&amp;#10;SNAKES run this world.  It's time to change this!! &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Unauthorized Storage of Toxic Agents,&amp;#10;U.S Senate Subcommittee on Intelligence..&amp;#10;https://archive.org/details/Church-Committee-Hearings-Volume1-Toxic-Agents/page/n23/mode/2up?q=cobra &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Baby Formula:&amp;#10;https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6027691/"
